NAME
    touch - create an empty file or update its modification time

SYNOPSIS
    touch <path>

DESCRIPTION
    Creates an empty file at <path> inside the shell sandbox if it does
    not exist, or updates its last-modified timestamp if it is an
    existing file. Refuses paths that name an existing directory.

EXAMPLES
    touch /Logs/scratch.txt

EXIT STATUS
    0   File created or timestamp updated.
    1   Missing path, path outside sandbox, path is a directory, or I/O
        error.

SEE ALSO
    cp(1), ls(1), nano(1)
